        <p class="marker rise">About the association</p>
        <h2 class="rise">Literature has readers in Ghana. It now has a professional home.</h2>
        <p class="rise">LITAG was unveiled by the Department of English at the University of Cape Coast in 2022, at a conference held in honour of three distinguished scholars of the Department, Prof. Naana Jane Opoku-Agyemang, Prof. Lawrence Owusu-Ansah and Prof. Kwadwo Opoku-Agyemang. Dr. Samuel Kwesi Nkansah, a Senior Lecturer in the Department, announced its formation on behalf of teachers, lecturers, tutors and researchers of literature working across the country.</p>
        <p class="rise">The association exists to gather that constituency in one place. Members meet to discuss literature, present research, test ideas before colleagues and set standards for the discipline as it is taught and examined in Ghana. Postgraduate students present alongside their supervisors, and senior scholars bring the next generation into the room with them.</p>
        <p class="rise">Membership reaches beyond the English department. Scholars, writers and researchers in Literature, Ghanaian Languages, French and English all belong here, which keeps the association's account of Ghanaian writing as wide as the writing itself.</p>
